# Simple, Readable Code

Prefer the shortest version that a beginner can still understand. If a line needs a comment to make sense, rewrite the code instead.

## Do

- Use clear names: `userName`, `isOpen`, `fetchPosts` — not `x`, `data2`, `doStuff`
- One idea per function. If it does two jobs, split it
- Keep functions short (aim under 30 lines)
- Use early returns to avoid nested `if` / `else`
- Delete unused variables, comments, and dead code
- Repeat a little rather than add a clever abstraction for a one-off

## Don't

- Don't nest more than 2 levels deep
- Don't write comments that restate the code (`// increment i`)
- Don't add types, wrappers, or helpers "just in case"
- Don't mix UI, data fetching, and business logic in one function

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — nested, vague names, extra else
function handle(d) {
  if (d) {
    if (d.ok) {
      return d.list;
    } else {
      return [];
    }
  } else {
    return [];
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD — flat, obvious names
function getPosts(response) {
  if (!response?.ok) return [];
  return response.list;
}
```
